  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Because Teferi's Ageless Insight is legendary, it's unlikely that one player will control two. However, if that happens, each card that player would draw after the first will result in four cards being drawn. If they control three, they draw eight cards, and so on.",
      "oracle_id": "1c9e1f75-73f0-4846-b53f-458a0984b1bb",
      "published_at": "2020-06-23",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a spell or ability causes you to put a card into your hand without specifically using the word \"draw,\" it's not a card drawn.",
      "oracle_id": "1c9e1f75-73f0-4846-b53f-458a0984b1bb",
      "published_at": "2020-06-23",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If two or more replacement effects would apply to a card-drawing event, the player drawing the card chooses the order in which to apply them.",
      "oracle_id": "1c9e1f75-73f0-4846-b53f-458a0984b1bb",
      "published_at": "2020-06-23",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Dredge can replace any card draw, not only the one during your draw step.",
      "oracle_id": "64446130-46d0-4129-a718-ed6a04218100",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect puts a card into your hand without specifically using the word \"draw,\" you're not drawing a card. Dredge can't replace this event.",
      "oracle_id": "64446130-46d0-4129-a718-ed6a04218100",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you're drawing multiple cards, each draw is performed one at a time. For example, if you're instructed to draw two cards and you replace the first draw with a dredge ability, another card with a dredge ability (including one that was milled by the first dredge ability) may be used to replace the second draw.",
      "oracle_id": "64446130-46d0-4129-a718-ed6a04218100",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once you've announced that you're applying a card's dredge ability to replace a draw, players can't take any actions until you've put that card into your hand and milled cards.",
      "oracle_id": "64446130-46d0-4129-a718-ed6a04218100",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "One card draw can't be replaced by multiple dredge abilities.",
      "oracle_id": "64446130-46d0-4129-a718-ed6a04218100",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can't attempt to use a dredge ability if you don't have enough cards in your library.",
      "oracle_id": "64446130-46d0-4129-a718-ed6a04218100",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the permanent was an Aura or an Equipment, it becomes unattached from whatever it was attached to.",
      "oracle_id": "7c3944fa-7c86-4979-85a9-86196aa94594",
      "published_at": "2014-11-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The enchanted permanent loses any card types, subtypes, and colors it previously had. It keeps any supertypes it had and its name remains unchanged. It gains “{T}: Add {G}” and loses all other abilities from its rules text. It will still have any abilities it gained from other effects.",
      "oracle_id": "7c3944fa-7c86-4979-85a9-86196aa94594",
      "published_at": "2014-11-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "After a spell with split second resolves (or otherwise leaves the stack), players may again cast spells and activate abilities before the next object on the stack resolves.",
      "oracle_id": "b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Casting a spell with split second won't affect spells and abilities that are already on the stack.",
      "oracle_id": "b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the resolution of a triggered ability involves casting a spell, that spell can't be cast if a spell with split second is on the stack.",
      "oracle_id": "b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Players may turn face-down creatures face up while a spell with split second is on the stack.",
      "oracle_id": "b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Players still get priority while a card with split second is on the stack; their options are just limited to mana abilities and certain special actions.",
      "oracle_id": "b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Split second doesn't stop triggered abilities from triggering, such as that of Chalice of the Void. If one does, its controller puts it on the stack and chooses targets for it, if any. Those abilities will resolve as normal.",
      "oracle_id": "b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because Alhammarret’s Archive is legendary, it’s unlikely that one player will control two. However, if that happens, life gained by that player will be multiplied by four. Three Archives will multiply that life gain by eight, and so on.",
      "oracle_id": "d5c4d36c-54b3-4149-906b-a57a670260fc",
      "published_at": "2015-06-22",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect would set your life total to a specific number that’s higher than your current life total, that effect would cause you to gain life equal to the difference. Alhammarret’s Archive will then double the amount of life that effect would cause you to gain. For example, if you have 3 life and an effect says that your life total “becomes 10,” your life total will actually become 17.",
      "oracle_id": "d5c4d36c-54b3-4149-906b-a57a670260fc",
      "published_at": "2015-06-22",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If two or more replacement effects would apply to a card-drawing event, the player drawing the card chooses the order in which to apply them.",
      "oracle_id": "d5c4d36c-54b3-4149-906b-a57a670260fc",
      "published_at": "2015-06-22",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In a Two-Headed Giant game, only the controller of Alhammarret’s Archive is affected by it. If that player’s teammate gains life, Alhammarret’s Archive will have no effect, even when that life gain is applied to the team’s shared life total.",
      "oracle_id": "d5c4d36c-54b3-4149-906b-a57a670260fc",
      "published_at": "2015-06-22",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Similarly, the effects of the last abilities of multiple Archives are cumulative. If you control two, you’ll draw four times the number of cards, and so on.",
      "oracle_id": "d5c4d36c-54b3-4149-906b-a57a670260fc",
      "published_at": "2015-06-22",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Although the draws are not optional, if an opponent doesn't draw a card, perhaps because a replacement effect replaced the draw with another effect, that player is not counted when determining how many cards you draw.",
      "oracle_id": "8b5cffd5-5db3-4151-9275-d91387554412",
      "published_at": "2022-06-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an opponent drew more than one card this way due to a replacement effect, you still draw only one card for that player.",
      "oracle_id": "8b5cffd5-5db3-4151-9275-d91387554412",
      "published_at": "2022-06-10",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": 1,
  "source": "Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"
}
